---
import DocsNav from "../../components/DocsNav.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import { docs, repositoryUrl } from "../../data/site";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Architecture | OrbitKV"
  description="OrbitKV compiler IR, physical design, block ownership, reclamation protocol, and NVIDIA backend boundaries."
  active="Architecture"
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Architecture</p>
    <h1>Temporal physical design for model state.</h1>
    <p>
      OrbitKV compiles future-read semantics into block lifetime, address,
      immutable view, and reclamation programs.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="docs-layout">
    <DocsNav active="Architecture" />
    <article class="prose">
      <h2>Pipeline</h2>
      <pre><code>{`Attention / state retention semantics
    -> Retention IR
    -> Lifetime / head stripes
    -> LayoutProgram
    -> PhysicalPlan
    -> immutable KVView
    -> SemanticDead ∧ ExecutionComplete
    -> backend commit
    -> reuse`}</code></pre>

      <h2>Generated layouts</h2>
      <table class="evidence-table-native">
        <thead><tr><th>Semantics</th><th>Layout</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Full</td><td><code>AppendOnly</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Sliding</td><td><code>Periodic</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Sink + Sliding</td><td><code>Pinned + Periodic</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Same Chunk</td><td><code>ResettableArena</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Per-head windows</td><td>Lifetime-normalized stripes</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>Safety</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Logical identity is separate from physical slot and generation.</li>
        <li>Address programs are the only logical addressing authority.</li>
        <li>Reuse requires semantic death, reader completion, and backend commit.</li>
        <li>Unsupported semantics and engine contracts fail closed.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Persistent capsules</h2>
      <p>
        Holt 0.9.2 is the sole persistent prefix catalog. OrbitKV durably writes
        immutable, content-addressed KV payload files first, then atomically
        publishes their Capsule manifests into one Holt tree. Restore validates model,
        tokenizer, adapter, StatePlan, prefix, payload, and component checksums.
      </p>
      <p>
        SGLang end-to-end qualification now covers compiler-proven pure-SWA
        live tails and GPT-OSS Full+SWA components. Hybrid restore keeps the
        complete Full history while moving only the final SWA window.
      </p>

      <h2>Capability levels</h2>
      <p>
        OrbitKV reports compiler, reference-runtime, GPU-primitive, engine-E2E,
        and production qualification separately. The{" "}
        <a href={`${repositoryUrl}/blob/main/docs/capability-matrix.md`}>
          Capability Matrix
        </a>{" "}
        is the normative boundary.
      </p>

      <h2>Records</h2>
      <div class="doc-grid">
        {docs.map((item) => (
          <div class="doc-card">
            <span>{item.key}</span>
            <h3>{item.name}</h3>
            <p>{item.detail}</p>
            <a href={item.href}>Open record →</a>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <div class="doc-note">
        <strong>Boundary.</strong>
        <p>
          The owning SGLang paths require ChunkCache with radix, speculation,
          overlap, and disaggregation disabled. Page16 pure SWA separately
          qualifies decode CUDA Graph. Capsule hydration is L4 only for the
          recorded pure-SWA and Full+SWA single-request workloads. VMM remains
          an isolated L3 primitive.
        </p>
        <a href={`${repositoryUrl}/blob/main/docs/h20-owning-vmm-validation-20260817.md`}>
          Full owning and VMM qualification
        </a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
